               common across memory systems. Recent advances have established a
               clear framework for Drosophila learning and revealed the
               following key operations: a) pattern separation, whereby dense
               combinatorial representations of odors are preprocessed to
               generate highly specific, nonoverlapping odor patterns used for
               learning; b) convergence, in which sensory information is
