  abstract  = "Feature learning is a crucial element for the performance of
               machine learning models. Recently, the exploration of feature
               learning in the context of kernel methods has led to the
               introduction of Recursive Feature Machines (RFMs). In this work,
               we connect diagonal RFMs to Automatic Relevance Determination
               (ARD) from the Gaussian process literature. We demonstrate that
               diagonal RFMs, similar to ARD, serve as a weighted covariate
               selection technique. However, they are trained using different
               paradigms: RFMs use recursive iterations of the so-called Average
               Gradient Outer Product, while ARD employs maximum likelihood
