              to a camera, or as a predictor of future stimuli. Addressing this
              dichotomy, we developed a biologically-detailed spiking retinal
              model trained on natural movies under metabolic-like constraints
              to either encode the present or to predict future scenes. Our
              findings reveal that when optimized for efficient prediction ∼ 100
              ms into the future, the model not only captures retina-like
