  journal       = "arXiv [cs.CV]",
  abstract      = "Generative Adversarial Nets (GANs) are very successful at
                   modeling distributions from given samples, even in the
                   high-dimensional case. However, their formulation is also
                   known to be hard to optimize and often not stable. While this
