               computations arise.",
  month     =  jun,
  year      =  2016,
  language  = "en"
}

@ARTICLE{Ammer2015-hm,
  title     = "{Functional Specialization of Neural Input Elements to the
               Drosophila on Motion Detector}",
  author    = "Ammer, Georg and Leonhardt, Aljoscha and Bahl, Armin and Dickson,
               Barry J and Borst, Alexander",
  journal   = "Curr. Biol.",
  publisher = "Elsevier",
  volume    =  25,
  number    =  17,
  pages     = "2247--2253",
  abstract  = "Detecting the direction of visual movement is fundamental for
               every sighted animal in order to navigate, avoid predators, or
               detect conspeciﬁcs. Algorithmic models of correlation-type motion
               detectors describe the underlying computation remarkably well
               [1–3]. They consist of two spatially separated input lines that
