  number   =  12,
  pages    = "5634--5639",
  abstract = "The visual systems of most species contain photoreceptors with
              distinct spectral sensitivities that allow animals to distinguish
              lights by their spectral composition. In Drosophila,
              photoreceptors R1–R6 have the same spectral sensitivity throughout
              the eye and are responsible for motion detection. In contrast,
