  number   =  12,
  pages    = "4910--4915",
  abstract = "Whether motion vision uses color contrast is a controversial issue
              that has been investigated in several species, from insects to
              humans. We used Drosophila to answer this question, monitoring the
              optomotor response to moving color stimuli in WT and genetic
              variants. In the fly eye, a motion channel (outer photoreceptors
