  journal  = "Neuron",
  volume   =  71,
  number   =  3,
  pages    = "555--564",
  abstract = "The process by which neural circuitry in the brain plans and
              executes movements is not well understood. Until recently, most
              available data were limited either to single-neuron
              electrophysiological recordings or to measures of aggregate field
              or metabolism. Neither approach reveals how individual neurons'
