              and the percentage of the local population activated were higher
              in the barrel column than above septa or in neighboring columns.
              Within the barrel column, mean response probability was highest in
              the center (0.4) and declined toward the barrel border. Neuronal
              pairs showed correlations in both spontaneous and sensory-evoked
              activity that depended on the location of the neurons. Correlation
