  number   =  7533,
  pages    = "200--204",
  abstract = "Establishing the hippocampal cellular ensemble that represents an
              animal's environment involves the emergence and disappearance of
              place fields in specific CA1 pyramidal neurons, and the
              acquisition of different spatial firing properties across the
              active population. While such firing flexibility and diversity
