  number    =  1,
  pages     = "229--243.e3",
  abstract  = "Many animals guide their movements using optic flow, the
               displacement of stationary objects across the retina caused by
               self-motion. How do animals selectively synthesize a global
               motion pattern from its local motion components? To what extent
               does this feature selectivity rely on circuit mechanisms versus
               dendritic processing? Here we used in vivo calcium imaging to
               identify pre- and postsynaptic mechanisms for processing local
               motion signals in global motion detection circuits in Drosophila.
