               pooling input from local motion detectors, T4/T5 neurons. We show
               that T4/T5 neurons suppress responses to adjacent local motion
               signals whereas LPTC dendrites selectively amplify spatiotemporal
               sequences of local motion signals consistent with preferred
               global patterns. We propose that sequential nonlinear suppression
               and amplification operations allow optic flow circuitry to
               simultaneously prevent saturating responses to local signals
