  abstract  = "SummaryMotion detection is nearly ubiquitous among visual
               animals. Simple ‘first-order' motion in an image is defined by
               spatiotemporal correlations in luminance, and is useful for tasks
               such as identifying a bright butterfly crawling on a tree. Humans
               additionally perceive ‘second-order' motion [1], defined by
