  number    =  1,
  pages     = "2--23",
  abstract  = "Ion channels are intimately involved in virtually every
               physiological process of consequence in humans. Their importance
               is underscored by the identification of numerous
               ``channelopathies'', human diseases caused by ion channel
               mutations. Ion Channels have consequently been viewed as fertile
               ground for drug discovery and, indeed, they represent one of the
