  journal       = "arXiv [cs.LG]",
  abstract      = "Training language models currently requires pre-determining a
                   fixed compute budget because the typical cosine learning rate
                   schedule depends on the total number of steps. In contrast,
                   the Warmup-Stable-Decay (WSD) schedule uses a constant
                   learning rate to produce a main branch of iterates that can
