  volume    =  99,
  number    =  2,
  pages     = "734--746",
  abstract  = "Learning and memory has been studied extensively in Drosophila
               using behavioral, molecular, and genetic approaches. These
               studies have identified the mushroom body as essential for the
               formation and retrieval of olfactory memories. We investigated
               odor responses of the principal neurons of the mushroom body, the
