  author        = "Wilson, Andrew Gordon and Izmailov, Pavel",
  journal       = "arXiv [cs.LG]",
  abstract      = "The key distinguishing property of a Bayesian approach is
                   marginalization, rather than using a single setting of
                   weights. Bayesian marginalization can particularly improve
                   the accuracy and calibration of modern deep neural networks,
                   which are typically underspecified by the data, and can
                   represent many compelling but different solutions. We show
