               complete (Fig. 1). This adaptation shifts theV/logI curves to
               higher intensities without changing their shape or slope (Fig.
               3). Adaptation is negligible at low intensities but with stronger
               adaptation range sensitivity changes approach proportionality to
               background increments (Fig. 7). 4. Lamina adaptation mechanisms
               adjust the LMCV/logI curve in response to new background levels
               within 200 ms, producing a phasic response waveform within which
