  volume    =  413,
  number    =  6852,
  pages     = "186--193",
  abstract  = "The brain's capacity to analyse and interpret information is
               limited ultimately by the input it receives. This sets a premium
               on information capacity of sensory receptors, which can be
               maximized by optimizing sensitivity, speed and reliability of
               response. Nowhere is selection pressure for information capacity
