  number    =  47,
  pages     = "29925--29936",
  abstract  = "Object-based attention describes the brain's capacity to
               prioritize one set of stimuli while ignoring others. Human
               research suggests that the binding of diverse stimuli into one
               attended percept requires phase-locked oscillatory activity in
               the brain. Even insects display oscillatory brain activity during
