  pages     = "1591--1594",
  abstract  = "Insects can estimate distance or time-to-contact of surrounding
               objects from locomotion-induced changes in their retinal position
               and/or size. Freely walking fruit flies (Drosophila melanogaster)
               use the received mixture of different distance cues to select the
