  abstract  = "Two dynamical models, proposed by Hopfield and Little to account
               for the collective behavior of neural networks, are analyzed. The
               long-time behavior of these models is governed by the statistical
               mechanics of infinite-range Ising spin-glass Hamiltonians.
               Certain configurations of the spin system, chosen at random,
