  number    =  10,
  pages     = "1568--1574",
  abstract  = "A general statistical description of the problem of learning from
               examples is presented. Learning in layered networks is posed as a
               search in the network parameter space for a network that
               minimizes an additive error function of a statistically
               independent examples. By imposing the equivalence of the minimum
               error and the maximum likelihood criteria for training the
