  pages    = "2025.07.31.667571",
  abstract = "Just as genomes revolutionized molecular genetics, connectomes
              (maps of neurons and synapses) are transforming neuroscience. To
              date, the only species with complete connectomes are worms1-3 and
              sea squirts4 (103-104 synapses). By contrast, the fruit fly is
